autonomic-agent (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Planned action: plain words in, audited actions out. This is the missing
    piece between the LLM and the Action channel -- until now the channel
    existed but nothing translated intent into calls it accepts.
    - `autonomicctl ask "..."`: the model proposes, the channel disposes
    - the tool list handed to the model is fetched live from autonomic-actd,
      never hardcoded in the planner, so the two cannot drift apart
    - every plan must pass structural checks (valid JSON, known action, known
      parameters, path inside the write allowlist) and every step must carry
      a reason; an unexplained write is refused
    - all steps are dry_run'd before ANY step is applied, because a
      half-applied plan leaves a machine that is neither where it was nor
      where you asked it to go
    - each step is verified immediately after apply; on failure everything
      stops and the already-applied steps are reported with their backups
  * Reversibility becomes a fact instead of a claim: backups now carry a
    sidecar recording where the file came from (the filename alone is
    ambiguous, since "_" is legal in Linux paths), and the new `file.restore`
    primitive puts them back. A reversible flag with no way back is a wish,
    not a capability.
  * `autonomicctl backups` lists every file the channel overwrote and prints
    the exact command to restore each one.
  * Backup filenames now carry microseconds: within the same second a second
    write silently overwrote the only copy of the previous contents.
  * scripts/mock-llm.py ships a fake OpenAI-compatible endpoint so the whole
    AI path can be verified without a real API key, and repeatedly.

 -- Autonomic OS <autonomic@localhost>  Sat, 11 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0800

autonomic-agent (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Power switch. The agent can now hold credentials for an OpenAI-compatible
    endpoint and tell you whether it actually works:
    - /etc/autonomic/agent.conf (0644) holds base_url/model/timeout
    - /etc/autonomic/credentials.env (0640 root:autonomic) holds the key only
    - the unit injects it with systemd LoadCredential=, so the secret never
      enters the process environment and cannot be grepped out of the journal
    - `autonomicctl setup` writes both (interactive, or --non-interactive for
      CI) and probes GET /models immediately
    - `autonomicctl llm` shows the config and re-checks connectivity
  * At boot the daemon now reports whether it has a usable credential, without
    calling anything. An unconfigured machine is still Autonomic OS -- it just
    has identity without a mind.
  * The Action channel (CHARTER 1.5), which is the reason any of the above
    matters. A key is useless if the agent cannot do anything with what it
    decides.
    The agent is deliberately NOT root. It now has a privileged companion,
    autonomic-actd, reachable only over a unix socket (0660 root:autonomic)
    whose peer credentials are read with SO_PEERCRED before the request is
    even parsed. There is no way to reduce this to a shell: four primitives
    (file.write, service.set, sysctl.set, self.test), each with a parameter
    schema and each gated by a write allowlist that refuses /etc/shadow,
    sudoers, ssh host keys and their neighbours outright.
  * Every action answers three questions instead of promising one:
    dry_run (what would change, touching nothing), apply (do it, journal it),
    verify (go look at the world again). `autonomicctl act` refuses to touch
    anything it has not shown you first, and always re-checks afterwards.
    When verify disagrees with apply, verify wins.
  * Every successful apply signals the counter daemon, so action_seq is now
    a real ledger of real changes rather than a decorative counter. Things
    done outside this channel do not move it -- that difference is precisely
    what drift detection is for.
  * No new runtime dependencies: urllib from the standard library only.

 -- Autonomic OS <contact@liguiyu.com>  Sat, 11 Oct 2026 00:20:00 +0800

autonomic-agent (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. M1: the agent gets an identity in the system --
    dedicated system user, hardened systemd unit, cgroup quota, own
    journal namespace, read-only world-version marker at
    /run/autonomic/world with drift detection.

